From 46fc7091889f89dc4cd5574b4f36e9740573a5d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:15:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Calendar Four/Five/Six sleep screens

Three new sleep-screen styles render a calendar grid of 4, 5, or 6 week
rows (7 columns, weeks start on Sunday). The grid begins on the Sunday of
the current week, so today always sits in the top row, drawn inverted in
a filled rounded cell. Known holidays (New Year's Day, Easter Sunday,
Christmas Day - see HolidayCalculator) get a dot marker.

- CrossPointSettings: SLEEP_SCREEN_MODE gains CALENDAR_FOUR/FIVE/SIX,
  appended before the COUNT sentinel so persisted indices keep meaning.
- SettingsList: labels via new StrIds; fromJson's enum clamp picks up the
  larger option count automatically, and the web settings UI enumerates
  options from the same list so it needs no changes (its hardcoded
  QUICK_RESUME=6 constant is untouched by appending).
- One parameterized renderer (CalendarSleepScreen::render, weeks count as
  the argument) backs all three styles; SleepActivity dispatches and owns
  the single HALF refresh, matching the other sleep renderers.
- HalClock: new getDateTime() exposes the RTC's UTC date; the calendar
  applies SETTINGS.clockUtcOffsetQ the same way formatTime does, with
  civil-date arithmetic that is exact across month/year boundaries.
- No RTC (X4) or failed RTC read falls back to the default sleep screen
  instead of guessing a date.
- I18n: new keys in english.yaml only (style names, weekday and month
  names); other languages fall back to English until translated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
